{"step_index":171,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T18:53:38Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Landing Page Design**\n\nI'm currently focused on the Netflix landing page design. I'm examining its structure, especially the call to action for login or signup. My aim is to extract the key elements that contribute to its effectiveness, and I'm planning to use these to create a similar landing page, while making the needed tweaks.\n\n\n**Reviewing Landing Page Structure**\n\nI've moved on to examining the StreamWave landing page. I've dissected the design into key components, specifically focusing on the header with its logo and \"Sign In\" button. I'm taking notes on the hero background, content (headline, subheading, and call to action), and the email input. I've also noted how the \"Get Started\" prompt integrates with the overall flow.\n\n\n**Implementing Hero Landing Section**\n\nI'm now integrating a dedicated Netflix-style hero landing section at the top, complete with top navigation (logo and \"Sign In\" button), overlay content (title, subtitle, and call-to-action form). The \"Sign In\" button will trigger an accessible sign-in demo modal, and the form will handle email input and a \"Get Started\" button. I'm focusing on responsiveness and user-friendliness for this section.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\">\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\">\\n    <title>StreamWave Entertainment | Unlimited Movies & Music</title>\\n    \\n    <!-- Favicon Links for Browser Tab Logo Icon -->\\n    <link rel=\\\"icon\\\" type=\\\"image/png\\\" href=\\\"/images/favicon.png\\\">\\n    <link rel=\\\"shortcut icon\\\" type=\\\"image/x-icon\\\" href=\\\"/favicon.ico\\\">\\n    <link rel=\\\"apple-touch-icon\\\" href=\\\"/images/favicon.png\\\">\\n\\n    <link rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\" href=\\\"/css/styles.css\\\">\\n    <link rel=\\\"preconnect\\\" href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\\\">\\n    <link rel=\\\"preconnect\\\" href=\\\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\\\" crossorigin>\\n    <link href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap\\\" rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\">\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n    <!-- Navigation Bar -->\\n    <header class=\\\"navbar\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"nav-container\\\">\\n            <a href=\\\"#landing\\\" class=\\\"brand\\\" aria-label=\\\"StreamWave Entertainment Home\\\">\\n                <img src=\\\"/images/streamwave-logo.png\\\" alt=\\\"StreamWave Entertainment Logo\\\" class=\\\"brand-logo-img\\\">\\n            </a>\\n\\n            <nav class=\\\"nav-links\\\" aria-label=\\\"Primary Navigation\\\">\\n                <a href=\\\"#catalogue\\\" class=\\\"nav-link\\\">Catalogue</a>\\n                <a href=\\\"/docs\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener\\\" class=\\\"nav-link developer-link\\\" title=\\\"Open API Documentation in Swagger\\\">\\n                    Developer <span class=\\\"ext-icon\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\">↗</span>\\n                </a>\\n                <button class=\\\"btn btn-primary btn-signin-nav\\\" onclick=\\\"window.streamWaveApp.openAuthModal()\\\">Sign In</button>\\n            </nav>\\n        </div>\\n    </header>\\n\\n    <main class=\\\"main-content\\\">\\n        <!-- Netflix-Style Landing Hero Section -->\\n        <section id=\\\"landing\\\" class=\\\"landing-hero\\\" aria-label=\\\"StreamWave Landing Page\\\">\\n            <div class=\\\"landing-backdrop\\\"></div>\\n            <div class=\\\"landing-\n<truncated 12886 bytes>","Description":"\"Add Netflix-style landing hero section, email form, and Sign In modal in public/index.html\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\dell\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\\\public\\\\index.html\"","toolAction":"\"Updatin