{"step_index":179,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T18:55:32Z","content":"I have created a Netflix-inspired landing page and Sign In system for **StreamWave Entertainment**.\n\n---\n\n### 🎬 Netflix-Style Landing Page Features\n\n1. **Netflix Hero Showcase**:\n   - Headline: *\"Unlimited Zimbabwean movies, music, and more\"*.\n   - Subtitle: *\"Stream anywhere. Serverless performance. Cancel anytime.\"*.\n   - Sub-prompt: *\"Ready to watch? Enter your email to get started or explore the catalogue.\"*.\n2. **Interactive Email Registration (`Get Started ›`)**:\n   - Entering an email and clicking **Get Started ›** smoothly scrolls down to the media catalogue with a personalized welcome toast badge.\n3. **Sign In Modal (`Sign In`)**:\n   - The top-right **Sign In** red button opens an accessible dark graphite modal with email/password input fields and a demo sign-in handler.\n4. **Branded Visual Design**:\n   - Rich dark vignette backdrop wallpaper with low-opacity media collage.\n   - Official StreamWave logo image in the header and browser tab favicon.\n   - **`▶ Watch`** and **`▶ Play`** button action labels."}
{"step_index":180,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:06:37Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nExtend the existing StreamWave FastAPI/Vercel project by adding an original landing page, simulated subscription-payment process and paid-member access control.\r\n\r\nDo not rebuild or break the existing catalogue, music player, five-second movie preview, playback logging, API documentation or Vercel configuration. Inspect the existing project before changing anything.\r\n\r\nThis is an academic demonstration. Do not integrate a real payment gateway, transfer money or collect real financial information.\r\n\r\nLANDING PAGE\r\n\r\n1. Make `/` the public landing page and the first page encountered by visitors.\r\n2. Use the existing StreamWave logo and dark graphite, white and red brand colours.\r\n3. Use the supplied streaming-service screenshot only as inspiration for visual hierarchy. Do not copy Netflix branding, wording, copyrighted posters or exact layout.\r\n4. Create an original hero section using existing StreamWave catalogue artwork with a dark overlay.\r\n5. Use this main copy:\r\n\r\n   * Heading: “Zimbabwe’s stories, music and movies — all in one place.”\r\n   * Supporting text: “Stream from US$2.99 per month. Cancel anytime.”\r\n   * Instruction: “Enter your email address to start your StreamWave membership.”\r\n6. Include:\r\n\r\n   * StreamWave logo.\r\n   * “Sign In” button.\r\n   * Email field.\r\n   * “Get Started” button.\r\n   * Brief benefits section.\r\n   * “How it works” section.\r\n   * Supported payment-method section.\r\n   * Academic-prototype footer notice.\r\n7. Keep the design professional, responsive and original. Avoid excessive gradients, glassmorphism, oversized rounded cards and generic AI styling.\r\n\r\nSUBSCRIPTION PLAN\r\n\r\nCreate one demonstration plan:\r\n\r\n* Name: StreamWave Monthly\r\n* Price: US$2.99 per month\r\n* Benefits: Full catalogue access, movie previews, music samples and access on desktop or mobile.\r\n* Store the price and plan name in one configuration location so they can be changed easily.\r\n\r\nCHECKOUT PAGE\r\n\r\nCreate a checkout page at `/checkout` containing:\r\n\r\n1. Customer email.\n<truncated 2463 bytes>\nry`.\r\n2. Only a valid demo-paid session may access `/library`.\r\n3. Unpaid users attempting to open `/library` must be redirected to the landing or checkout page.\r\n4. Protect these existing endpoints using a reusable FastAPI dependency:\r\n\r\n   * `/api/media`\r\n   * `/api/media/{media_id}`\r\n   * `/api/play-events`\r\n5. Keep `/api/health` and `/docs` publicly accessible for assessment.\r\n6. When a paid session is active:\r\n\r\n   * Show the customer email or “Demo Member”.\r\n   * Show a “Sign Out” button.\r\n   * Allow catalogue browsing.\r\n   * Allow music samples.\r\n   * Allow the five-second movie preview.\r\n7. Signing out must clear the membership cookie and return the user to the landing page.\r\n8. Add a clearly labelled “Reset Demonstration” control for assessment purposes.\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT LIMITATION\r\n\r\nThe current video and audio samples may remain public static demonstration assets. Do not claim that this prototype provides DRM or fully secure commercial media protection. Document that a production system would require private object storage, authenticated delivery URLs and digital-rights controls.\r\n\r\nTESTS\r\n\r\nAdd automated tests covering:\r\n\r\n* Landing page is publicly accessible.\r\n* Checkout page is publicly accessible.\r\n* Unpaid user cannot access `/library`.\r\n* Unpaid user cannot retrieve protected catalogue data.\r\n* Invalid payment method is rejected.\r\n* Invalid email is rejected.\r\n* Successful EcoCash simulation.\r\n* Successful Visa simulation.\r\n* Successful MasterCard simulation.\r\n* Successful simulation sets an access cookie.\r\n* Demo-paid user can open `/library`.\r\n* Demo-paid user can access catalogue endpoints.\r\n* Logout clears access.\r\n* Existing catalogue, filtering, music and movie-preview tests continue to pass.\r\n\r\nRun all tests and fix every failure. Finish by reporting files changed, endpoints added, actual test results and remaining limitations. Do not report success without testing.\r\n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-25T21:06:37+02:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":181,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:06:37Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Architecture Details**\n\nI'm currently diving into the architectural overview and requirements for the StreamWave serverless platform. Focusing on the need to extend the FastAPI/Vercel project, I'm identifying key areas for expansion and integration. The goal is a clear understanding before proceeding with further development.\n\n\n**Designing Landing Page Elements**\n\nI've been working on the public-facing landing page, specifically the `/` route. My focus is on the hero section: crafting compelling text (\"Zimbabwe's stories, music, and movies - all in one place\") and incorporating the StreamWave logo. I want a clean, professional UI, avoiding generic AI-generated designs. I'm also ensuring the \"Sign In\" button, email field, and \"Get Started\" button are prominently placed. I've designed a clear structure for the benefits and \"How it works\" sections. I am also planning the simulated checkout page at `/checkout`.\n\n\n**Implementing Payment Simulation**\n\nI'm now implementing the Visa/MasterCard simulation. My recent progress involves defining demo cards with masked values, simulating payment authorization, and ensuring only essential data (`method`, `plan_id`/`plan_name`, `email`) is sent to the backend. Card details are never transmitted or stored. I'm focusing on a seamless user experience for the demo payment flow.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"list_dir","args":{"DirectoryPath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\dell\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\"","toolAction":"\"Listing workspace files\"","toolSummary":"\"Listing workspace files\""}}]}
